    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "grief doesn't really change the fact that the math doesn't add up. i look at the last two decades and i just see a massive deficit. i'm 45 now. i've spent my entire prime being a slave to a dream that just evaporated. it feels like i've been playing a game where the rules changed mid-way through and now i'm just stuck in a losing position. what's the logic in just continuing to play when you know you're already bankrupt?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
